  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>Tokenized stocks distributed value rose 13.9% over 30D:</strong> Tokenized equity distributed value at $3.69B (13.9% higher over 30D) shows the early lane still adding balance sheet on a small set of platforms. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/11/02/nyse-taps-wall-street-giant-broadridge-to-bring-shareholder-voting-onto-blockchain-rails\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">NYSE tokenized stock plans take shape as four more transfer agents join</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Tokenized stocks remain an early-stage lane:</strong> liquidity and scale are still concentrated in a small set of platforms/networks. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/11/02/nvidia-costco-and-nike-join-pushback-against-okx-ice-tokenized-stock-plans\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Nvidia, Costco and Nike join pushback against OKX\u2013ICE tokenized stock plans</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Tokenized equities remain an early access market:</strong> Liquidity and scale stay concentrated until broker distribution and custody plumbing can support broader trading. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/11/02/standard-chartered-debuts-tokenized-deposits-in-hong-kong-for-corporate-clients\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Standard Chartered debuts tokenized deposits in Hong Kong for corporate clients</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Regulatory framing still decides product access:</strong> Securities and broker-rule constraints often set the pace more than listing count, so near-term share stays tied to venues that can actually distribute products. Related: <a href=\"https://cointelegraph.com/news/crypto-com-hong-kong-app-shutdown-license-pending?utm_source=rss_feed&amp;utm_medium=rss&amp;utm_campaign=rss_partner_inbound\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Crypto.com to withdraw Hong Kong consumer app citing regulatory changes</a> (CoinTelegraph).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
